WEBVTT

00:02.390 --> 00:04.880
Seeing Midori-senpai, I think to myself...

00:05.780 --> 00:11.710
This must be the concert 
band that she'd imagined.

01:41.540 --> 01:43.250
I'm home.

01:44.390 --> 01:45.960
What is this?

01:46.470 --> 01:49.170
Someone from work gave it to me.

01:49.170 --> 01:52.880
They caught it at a festival, 
but they can't take care of it.

01:52.880 --> 01:54.440
Huh.

01:55.400 --> 01:59.560
<i>You have a diverse career in 
both movies and stage plays.</i>

01:59.560 --> 02:01.610
<i>Why did you choose to become an actor?</i>

02:02.020 --> 02:05.630
<i>Well... I dunno, I guess.</i>

02:05.630 --> 02:08.030
<i>You don't know?</i>

02:07.340 --> 02:08.650
Kumiko.

02:08.030 --> 02:12.140
<i>It's just that I can't think 
of a particular occasion.</i>

02:10.770 --> 02:12.120
Yeah?

02:12.120 --> 02:13.960
Have you decided what you're 
doing after high school?

02:12.140 --> 02:15.600
<i>If I had to say, it might have been 
when my senior forced me to...</i>

02:14.740 --> 02:15.600
Not yet.

02:15.600 --> 02:18.610
If there's something you want to do, say it.

02:18.610 --> 02:20.190
I won't force anything on you.

02:20.910 --> 02:24.860
You could talk to your sister if 
you're having trouble deciding.

02:24.860 --> 02:25.280
Eh?

02:26.850 --> 02:28.660
Is something wrong?

02:29.050 --> 02:30.470
She's your sister.

02:34.880 --> 02:38.800
<b>Episode 5</b>

02:34.880 --> 02:38.800
<b>Twilight for Two</b>

02:38.800 --> 02:41.600
You plan on going to a public college, huh?

02:41.600 --> 02:42.470
Yeah.

02:42.470 --> 02:43.540
What about you, Hazuki-chan?

02:43.540 --> 02:45.170
I haven't decided yet.

02:45.170 --> 02:48.740
I'm starting to feel the 
pressure to decide, though.

02:48.740 --> 02:50.450
Right?

02:50.450 --> 02:51.960
Career plans, huh?

02:52.760 --> 02:54.110
You still haven't decided?

02:54.490 --> 02:57.630
I don't even know what I want to do yet.

02:57.630 --> 02:58.690
What about music school?

02:58.690 --> 03:01.550
Yoroizuka-senpai got accepted, too.

03:01.550 --> 03:03.090
That again?

03:03.090 --> 03:07.360
I don't think I can make 
a living off of music.

03:07.590 --> 03:10.390
Meaning that you would if you could?

03:11.830 --> 03:17.380
More like, I can't picture myself 
being a working adult.

03:17.380 --> 03:19.790
Don't you have any dreams for the future?

03:19.790 --> 03:20.670
Not really.

03:20.670 --> 03:22.560
Never? In your whole life?

03:22.560 --> 03:23.310
Never.

03:23.740 --> 03:26.720
I'm not like you. I can't think of anything.

03:27.550 --> 03:28.760
Then...

03:28.760 --> 03:30.890
What do you live for?

03:33.990 --> 03:38.270
I get it. You've been planning to be a 
professional musician your whole life.

03:38.850 --> 03:40.150
True.

03:41.320 --> 03:44.020
I shouldn't have asked you.

03:44.020 --> 03:45.980
Come on, that's mean.

03:45.980 --> 03:47.620
It's not mean!

03:48.550 --> 03:53.280
Oh yeah, I want to come to a decision on 
that issue at the exec meeting tomorrow.

03:53.280 --> 03:54.580
What issue?

03:54.880 --> 03:55.840
Auditions.

03:55.840 --> 03:57.050
Oh.

03:57.050 --> 03:57.710
Right.

03:58.120 --> 03:59.720
We have to decide.

04:00.300 --> 04:06.720
Congrats
 Kansai 
Competition
 Boys'
 High
 School
Broadcast
 Contest
 Announcement
 Team

04:01.120 --> 04:04.450
<i>The concert band competition 
happens only once a year.</i>

04:04.450 --> 04:07.620
<i>The audition to decide 
who will be participating</i>

04:07.620 --> 04:11.720
<i>is one of the most important 
activities for the club's members.</i>

04:12.060 --> 04:15.470
<i>Reina's words reminded me of that fact</i>

04:15.470 --> 04:20.840
<i>and completely erased my
thoughts about career planning.</i>

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Summer Break

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
October\h\h\h\h\h\h\hSeptember\h\h\h\h\h\hAugust\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hJuly\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hJune

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
School 
Trip

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Auditions?

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Exams 
(Part 1)

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Kyoto
Competition

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Camp 
3 days

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Kansai
Competition

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Culture
Festival

04:18.980 --> 04:23.110
Exams
(Part 2)

04:21.740 --> 04:23.110
Nationals

04:22.270 --> 04:24.630
The problem is the auditions.

04:24.630 --> 04:26.430
Considering the Kyoto Competition is coming,

04:26.430 --> 04:29.880
I want to get them done by the end 
of June, like Taki-sensei suggested.

04:29.880 --> 04:32.360
What if we do them in July instead?

04:32.360 --> 04:33.820
Why?

04:33.820 --> 04:38.360
Some people said we chose our members too 
early last year, and people let their guard down.

04:38.360 --> 04:40.810
I thought it might be 
good to shake things up.

04:40.810 --> 04:42.890
I agree with that.

04:42.880 --> 04:46.680
Exec Notes

04:42.890 --> 04:47.840
We need to change something if we 
want to do better than last year.

04:49.170 --> 04:50.670
Something...

04:50.670 --> 04:55.350
Something that'll make people 
treat practice with more urgency.

04:57.080 --> 05:01.260
We could try learning from what 
the successful schools do.

05:01.260 --> 05:06.130
Come to think of it, Mayu-chan said 
Seira Girls' Academy holds an audition

05:06.130 --> 05:07.890
for each competition.

05:07.890 --> 05:09.080
Really?

05:09.080 --> 05:10.050
Yeah.

05:10.050 --> 05:12.010
Something like this.

05:13.300 --> 05:15.450
We're starting from scratch each time?

05:15.450 --> 05:16.580
Yeah, yeah.

05:16.580 --> 05:22.340
Audition

05:16.580 --> 05:22.340
Audition

05:16.580 --> 05:22.340
Audition

05:17.170 --> 05:20.610
That would definitely keep 
the club members focused.

05:20.610 --> 05:26.830
It might be a lot of work 
for Taki-sensei, though.

05:26.840 --> 05:28.930
<b>Staff 
Office</b>

05:27.440 --> 05:28.920
Understood.

05:31.300 --> 05:35.980
If you believe that's for the 
best, I have no objections.

05:35.980 --> 05:37.180
Really?

05:37.550 --> 05:38.460
Yes.

05:38.460 --> 05:42.060
I've been thinking it'd be 
better to make some changes.

05:42.060 --> 05:44.650
I believe it's worth trying.

05:45.210 --> 05:49.100
Isn't it too much of a 
burden on you, though?

05:49.870 --> 05:53.100
That's for me to decide.

05:53.100 --> 05:54.410
Don't worry about that.

05:54.410 --> 05:58.060
You're going to need to be ready 
for your own burdens, too.

05:59.460 --> 06:03.460
Audition
 Kyoto Competition

05:59.990 --> 06:07.670
Basically, if we do make it to the 
Nationals, we'll have three auditions in total.

06:07.670 --> 06:09.900
Three auditions? That's like...

06:09.900 --> 06:11.510
An audition each time.

06:11.830 --> 06:13.970
Please raise your hand 
if you have a question.

06:14.900 --> 06:16.820
Yes, Hisaishi-san.

06:16.820 --> 06:19.280
What about the solos?

06:19.280 --> 06:22.910
Are we going to be choosing 
new soloists each time, too?

06:23.810 --> 06:25.040
That's correct.

06:25.040 --> 06:25.900
I see.

06:26.180 --> 06:30.560
So we're going to be choosing the best 
members based on how they improve.

06:30.560 --> 06:33.310
Kitauji is an absolute meritocracy.

06:33.310 --> 06:35.920
That's the best approach.

06:35.920 --> 06:37.250
I agree.

06:37.250 --> 06:38.820
No objections.

06:38.820 --> 06:40.490
Thank you.

06:43.360 --> 06:44.310
Um...

06:44.310 --> 06:45.700
Kuroe-san?

06:46.160 --> 06:48.120
No, I just...

06:48.120 --> 06:51.790
Am I auditioning, too?

06:53.590 --> 06:56.300
You're a club member,
so it follows that you will.

06:58.440 --> 06:59.800
I see.

07:03.030 --> 07:05.510
Okay, first-years, gather 'round!

07:05.510 --> 07:06.660
We're already here.

07:06.660 --> 07:08.180
From the Yayoi period.

07:10.000 --> 07:13.290
I'm going to talk about the competitions.

07:13.290 --> 07:14.410
Okay.

07:14.410 --> 07:18.740
There are three concert band competitions.

07:14.590 --> 07:17.720
There are solo parts for contrabass 
too, aren't there, Motomu-kun?

07:17.720 --> 07:18.750
Are you going for them?

07:18.740 --> 07:23.410
The Kyoto Prefectural, the Kansai 
Regionals and the Nationals.

07:19.060 --> 07:20.210
Of course not.

07:20.210 --> 07:21.890
Midori-senpai's obviously going to...

07:21.350 --> 07:22.680
Chop!

07:23.100 --> 07:24.710
What was that for?

07:23.410 --> 07:27.900
The judges assign each performance 
a gold, silver or bronze evaluation,

07:24.710 --> 07:26.250
Don't be like that!

07:26.250 --> 07:29.200
Be ambitious, young one! Chop!

07:27.900 --> 07:31.880
and several of the gold winners are 
nominated to go to the next competition.

07:29.200 --> 07:30.590
Stop it.

07:29.200 --> 07:32.350
Motomu-kun's been talking more lately.

07:30.590 --> 07:32.700
Double chop!

07:32.350 --> 07:33.170
Has he?

07:34.270 --> 07:37.910
Do you hate auditions <i>that</i> much?

07:37.910 --> 07:39.730
More like...

07:39.730 --> 07:41.480
I wonder if I could forfeit.

07:41.480 --> 07:42.660
Why would you do that?

07:42.660 --> 07:47.060
If I compete, I'm taking up a slot.

07:47.060 --> 07:51.670
I think someone who's been at Kitauji 
for longer should have priority.

07:52.110 --> 07:55.950
That would mean the third 
years take priority.

07:56.560 --> 07:58.450
Kitauji is meritocratic,

07:58.450 --> 08:02.200
and we audition for the 
best members in each part,

08:02.200 --> 08:04.500
and we compete with the best team.

08:04.500 --> 08:07.040
You're a Kitauji club member, 
aren't you, Mayu-chan?

08:08.310 --> 08:13.680
Were you maybe forfeiting the 
auditions at Seira Girls', too?

08:13.680 --> 08:15.120
No way.

08:15.120 --> 08:18.000
I was in Seira from first-year, though.

08:18.000 --> 08:20.640
And everyone appreciated 
it when I worked at it.

08:20.940 --> 08:23.380
That's no different at Kitauji.

08:25.030 --> 08:26.520
Really?

08:28.360 --> 08:29.090
Yeah.

08:33.660 --> 08:35.110
Sorry.

08:35.110 --> 08:37.150
I'm going to play on my own for a bit.

08:40.140 --> 08:44.610
Trumpet and euph have a soli together 
in the selection piece, right?

08:44.610 --> 08:45.620
Yeah.

08:46.290 --> 08:50.760
Looks like you and Kousaka-senpai 
are going to be doing it.

08:53.200 --> 08:57.430
Why do you have to pile on 
like that, Kanade-chan?

08:57.430 --> 09:00.390
The person who auditions 
the best is playing.

09:00.780 --> 09:02.400
That's all there is to it.

09:03.950 --> 09:05.390
Fine.

09:06.110 --> 09:10.150
<i>The performing members are chosen by 
audition, regardless of their school year.</i>

09:10.150 --> 09:14.410
<i>And it was dawning on me that 
that wouldn't be so simple.</i>

09:16.870 --> 09:20.900
I took a shot asking Kousaka-senpai, 
but she turned me down.

09:20.900 --> 09:22.180
For the Agata Festival?

09:22.180 --> 09:22.860
Yeah.

09:22.860 --> 09:25.080
Of course she did. She has 
entrance exams coming up.

09:25.080 --> 09:26.310
You're right.

09:26.310 --> 09:27.310
I'm dead.

09:27.310 --> 09:27.990
What's up?

09:30.140 --> 09:31.540
Nothing.

09:32.120 --> 09:34.390
Oh, right, do you have a minute?

09:35.350 --> 09:36.730
Motomu-kun?

09:36.730 --> 09:40.980
Well, you remember he was arguing with 
some people from Ryusei at SunFes?

09:40.980 --> 09:43.340
I thought maybe he's having 
a hard time opening up.

09:44.240 --> 09:47.340
He should be fine, now.

09:47.340 --> 09:48.670
Really?

09:48.670 --> 09:52.130
I think inviting him to the Agata 
Festival is a good idea, though.

09:52.130 --> 09:53.230
Yeah?

09:53.230 --> 09:54.890
I'll do that, then.

09:57.090 --> 09:58.230
Shuichi.

09:58.710 --> 10:00.010
Thanks.

10:01.050 --> 10:02.950
I'm vice president.

10:03.370 --> 10:05.210
I should have done this sooner.

10:06.500 --> 10:08.410
Did Reina tell you that?

10:08.410 --> 10:09.540
Nope.

10:09.540 --> 10:11.540
But she probably will.

10:14.920 --> 10:16.670
I'm playing
the soli!!

10:20.090 --> 10:21.270
Kumiko-chan.

10:23.100 --> 10:24.360
Sorry.

10:24.360 --> 10:25.680
Did I startle you?

10:25.680 --> 10:27.220
Y-Yeah.

10:27.220 --> 10:28.300
You scared me.

10:28.300 --> 10:29.610
Sorry.

10:29.610 --> 10:32.520
I couldn't find a place 
to practice on my own.

10:32.520 --> 10:36.950
People get a bit territorial, huh?

10:37.870 --> 10:39.220
I'll help you find a spot.

10:39.220 --> 10:40.270
No, it's fine.

10:40.270 --> 10:41.730
I don't want to waste your time.

10:41.730 --> 10:43.090
Although...

10:43.790 --> 10:45.990
There's something I want to ask you.

10:50.180 --> 10:52.090
What's the Agata Festival?

10:54.170 --> 10:55.720
Oh, right.

10:55.720 --> 10:58.710
Everyone talks about it. It sounds fun.

10:58.710 --> 11:02.990
People say it's a weird nighttime ritual, 
but it's just a normal festival.

11:04.260 --> 11:05.350
That sounds fun.

11:06.660 --> 11:10.770
Do you have plans to go with someone?

11:13.220 --> 11:16.710
Would you like to go together?

11:18.180 --> 11:19.440
With me?

11:20.970 --> 11:23.280
No?

11:25.600 --> 11:29.790
Sorry, I already have 
plans with other people.

11:30.440 --> 11:31.790
Ah.

11:31.790 --> 11:35.480
Sorry. You should come hang 
out with us sometime.

11:35.480 --> 11:37.440
We can invite Hazuki-chan and them.

11:38.340 --> 11:39.150
Okay.

11:40.480 --> 11:42.440
<i>I'd gone and lied.</i>

11:42.900 --> 11:44.290
The soli part?

11:45.810 --> 11:47.320
Oh, yeah.

11:47.740 --> 11:49.640
Mind if I join you?

11:49.640 --> 11:51.560
I'll play the trumpet part.

11:54.730 --> 11:55.780
Yeah.

11:55.780 --> 11:56.810
Sure.

12:02.560 --> 12:03.830
Kumiko.

12:14.730 --> 12:16.550
Clear and bouncy.

12:16.550 --> 12:19.450
Loud but not obnoxious at all.

12:19.450 --> 12:21.660
Seira Girls' is something else.

12:22.010 --> 12:25.250
I heard you practicing 
the soli with Kuroe-san.

12:25.250 --> 12:26.350
Reina?!

12:26.350 --> 12:27.510
Were you listening?

12:28.620 --> 12:30.460
Our underclassmen were talking about it.

12:32.080 --> 12:36.410
Speaking of underclassmen, you got 
invited to the Agata Festival, didn't you?

12:36.410 --> 12:37.370
Yeah.

12:37.370 --> 12:38.440
I turned her down, though.

12:38.820 --> 12:39.970
Why?

12:40.440 --> 12:42.950
She'd start talking about 
taking the entire part.

12:42.950 --> 12:45.160
I don't like doing stuff like that.

12:45.570 --> 12:47.190
Huh.

12:51.830 --> 12:53.500
What about you?

12:55.020 --> 12:57.100
I don't have any plans, really.

12:58.230 --> 12:59.320
What?

13:00.650 --> 13:01.770
Nothing.

13:02.260 --> 13:03.460
In that case...

13:04.990 --> 13:06.960
Wanna come to my place this year?

13:07.690 --> 13:09.180
Your place?

13:14.980 --> 13:18.860
Student-Teacher
 Meeting

13:14.980 --> 13:18.860
Quiet!!

13:15.370 --> 13:18.860
In other words, you have 
no vision for your future.

13:19.150 --> 13:20.010
Yes.

13:20.010 --> 13:22.520
I've always been kind of passive.

13:22.520 --> 13:25.060
Truthfully, a lot of students are that way.

13:25.060 --> 13:28.560
You don't need to hurry to cross out 
options for what you want to be.

13:28.890 --> 13:32.820
But don't use indecision 
as an excuse to be lazy.

13:33.300 --> 13:38.130
Develop a habit of looking for reasons not to 
act, and before you know it, you'll be stuck.

13:38.840 --> 13:41.470
Am I being scolded right now?

13:44.590 --> 13:46.350
Some information on college.

13:46.350 --> 13:48.040
You ought to skim through it.

13:49.510 --> 13:54.090
Why did you decide to become 
a teacher, Michie-sensei?

13:55.360 --> 13:58.420
Because I wanted a stable job, I suppose.

13:58.760 --> 14:00.320
That's it?

14:00.320 --> 14:01.720
Yeah, that's it.

14:01.720 --> 14:05.060
But now, I think this is the best job ever.

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
June 
Personal Goals

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
Update 
personal best

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
Play in 
the Prefectural!!

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
Do better
 on exams

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
Stop sleeping 
during class!

14:05.070 --> 14:08.660
Be more unique

14:06.090 --> 14:08.670
Having a goal and working 
towards it is fine.

14:09.070 --> 14:12.070
But most of the time,
things don't go as planned.

14:12.370 --> 14:14.580
Overthinking it isn't good, either.

14:14.580 --> 14:15.980
I understand.

14:16.700 --> 14:20.130
But I'm not sure I should be 
deciding without any goals.

14:22.220 --> 14:23.670
Was that funny?

14:23.670 --> 14:24.770
No.

14:24.770 --> 14:30.740
I was just thinking that doesn't sound 
like something a passive person would say.

14:33.520 --> 14:35.770
Kumiko-senpai!

14:35.770 --> 14:37.690
You're going, too, right?

14:37.690 --> 14:38.790
To the Agata Festival!

14:38.790 --> 14:41.490
I heard the trumpets decided to go together.

14:41.490 --> 14:43.610
So the bass section should go together, too.

14:43.610 --> 14:44.860
I see.

14:44.860 --> 14:46.310
But...

14:46.310 --> 14:50.660
Mama-senpai said she's going with 
Tsubame-senpai when I asked her earlier,

14:50.660 --> 14:53.910
so she's fine as long as we're okay 
with Tsubame-senpai coming along.

14:55.830 --> 14:57.510
Whoa, that's an old camera.

14:57.800 --> 14:59.790
Yeah. It's a film camera.

14:59.790 --> 15:01.070
I like photography.

15:01.070 --> 15:02.480
That's so nice.

15:02.480 --> 15:03.880
I'll dress up for the festival, then.

15:04.310 --> 15:05.590
You're coming, right?

15:06.650 --> 15:09.590
Sorry, I already have other plans...

15:11.230 --> 15:12.780
Is it Shuichi?!

15:12.780 --> 15:13.590
No way!

15:14.120 --> 15:15.850
What about you, Motomu-paisen?

15:16.290 --> 15:21.110
Sorry, I'm going to be going with the vice 
president and some other guy members.

15:21.110 --> 15:23.020
That's a first.

15:23.020 --> 15:25.320
You going places with people?

15:25.630 --> 15:26.990
Wanna come, Hisaishi?

15:26.990 --> 15:28.400
I'll tell Senpai.

15:29.370 --> 15:33.470
Sadly, I promised Ririka we'd go together.

15:34.530 --> 15:37.020
You, too, Kanade-senpai?!

15:37.020 --> 15:39.920
Who's going to go with me, then?!

15:37.760 --> 15:45.350
<i>The unique hype that comes before a festival 
was soon followed by the festival itself.</i>

15:39.920 --> 15:40.990
You've got me.

15:47.350 --> 15:48.830
Kumiko!

15:50.040 --> 15:51.520
Sorry I'm late.

15:51.520 --> 15:52.750
Did you find your way all right?

15:52.750 --> 15:53.480
Yeah.

15:53.480 --> 15:54.990
Do you not want to go to the festival?

15:54.990 --> 15:56.470
Do you?

15:56.470 --> 15:57.880
No.

15:57.880 --> 16:00.650
I was hoping to do something 
different from everyone else.

16:01.210 --> 16:02.350
Same.

16:07.090 --> 16:08.440
Wow.

16:09.350 --> 16:10.720
It's big.

16:10.720 --> 16:12.500
Dad's not home today.

16:12.500 --> 16:13.710
Work?

16:13.710 --> 16:14.550
Yeah.

16:14.550 --> 16:16.480
I think he's in Austria right now.

16:16.480 --> 16:17.660
Kumiko-chan.

16:17.660 --> 16:18.420
Come in.

16:18.710 --> 16:20.710
I haven't seen you since the performance.

16:20.710 --> 16:21.750
Right.

16:21.750 --> 16:23.070
Nice to thank you.

16:23.070 --> 16:24.410
Relax a little.

16:25.010 --> 16:26.910
Over here, everyone.

16:26.910 --> 16:28.330
Smile!

16:29.890 --> 16:31.520
Okay, got it.

16:31.970 --> 16:34.140
I'm glad it didn't rain.

16:32.790 --> 16:34.140
Midori-senpai.

16:34.610 --> 16:35.880
Hey!

16:35.880 --> 16:38.070
Come take pictures with us!

16:39.490 --> 16:42.860
Okay, eyes on me.

16:46.800 --> 16:48.810
Kumiko isn't here.

16:48.810 --> 16:50.310
Ah. Oh.

16:50.310 --> 16:51.830
Scooch over just a little!

16:51.830 --> 16:52.720
A little more!

16:52.720 --> 16:53.780
Little more!

16:53.780 --> 16:54.610
Okay.

16:55.490 --> 16:57.590
All right, here we go.

16:57.590 --> 16:59.370
Say, "cheese"!

17:06.000 --> 17:07.690
That was amazing.

17:07.690 --> 17:09.740
Are your dinners always like that?

17:09.740 --> 17:10.870
Of course not.

17:10.870 --> 17:12.900
Only when we have guests.

17:13.310 --> 17:14.980
That was so delicious.

17:16.500 --> 17:18.670
How was the student-teacher meeting?

17:20.130 --> 17:22.030
Oh, well...

17:22.030 --> 17:25.840
I thought I was going to get 
yelled at, but I didn't really.

17:25.840 --> 17:28.040
"You shouldn't overthink it," she says.

17:28.040 --> 17:29.610
Why not music school?

17:29.610 --> 17:33.510
You really want me to go to music school.

17:33.510 --> 17:35.560
You keep saying you can't decide.

17:37.070 --> 17:40.570
To be honest, I don't think 
music school would ever happen.

17:41.490 --> 17:46.500
I think it's for people who want 
to keep performing as adults.

17:46.820 --> 17:49.830
I don't think that's necessarily true.

17:49.830 --> 17:51.860
I don't want to, though.

17:51.860 --> 17:54.660
I think it would be disrespectful of 
me to go with my current attitude.

17:54.660 --> 17:56.840
A normal university, then?

17:57.370 --> 18:03.390
I guess that's the normal thing to do if 
you're like me and you have no goals.

18:04.400 --> 18:05.610
I see.

18:05.880 --> 18:08.990
But I don't want to do that either.

18:09.820 --> 18:12.570
I feel like I'll go back to 
how I was in middle school.

18:13.410 --> 18:17.430
Just going along with whatever people say.

18:17.430 --> 18:20.070
Going through life without 
questioning anything.

18:21.980 --> 18:26.620
It's easy to put it off,
but I don't think I should.

18:27.830 --> 18:29.500
I need to find something.

18:30.540 --> 18:32.250
Can't it be music?

18:39.260 --> 18:41.590
Our selection piece this year.

18:41.590 --> 18:46.240
This piece is supposed to depict a 
year with the composer's father.

18:46.780 --> 18:51.270
I heard each movement is 
one of the four seasons.

18:52.220 --> 18:55.130
It's pretty epic, huh?

18:55.520 --> 18:57.460
That's the first impression.

18:58.780 --> 19:03.370
But I think it's a nice, simple 
piece once you listen carefully.

19:03.370 --> 19:05.290
Like the third movement.

19:05.530 --> 19:06.260
Yeah.

19:06.260 --> 19:08.240
The euph-'pet soli.

19:08.790 --> 19:09.690
Yeah.

19:09.690 --> 19:14.340
You can sense the winter coming,
but there's still a pleasant light.

19:14.340 --> 19:16.340
I thought the same thing.

19:20.540 --> 19:21.560
Kumiko...

19:22.660 --> 19:23.880
Wanna play?

19:23.880 --> 19:25.810
I have instruments in the studio.

19:27.300 --> 19:30.800
You can play with me if you can 
play with Kuroe-san, can't you?

19:34.300 --> 19:36.900
So this is where you're always playing.

19:36.900 --> 19:37.890
Yeah.

19:43.700 --> 19:45.520
Mayu-chan's good, huh?

19:46.210 --> 19:48.790
I like your playing better.

19:49.580 --> 19:50.750
Okay, let's go.

21:08.990 --> 21:13.420
I want to play this soli 
with you at the Nationals.

21:16.410 --> 21:17.590
Same.

21:24.840 --> 21:27.130
The festival should be about over.

21:29.020 --> 21:31.040
Wanna come over again?

21:32.620 --> 21:33.720
Can I?

21:33.720 --> 21:35.130
If it's all right with you.

21:35.130 --> 21:36.720
Of course it is.

21:37.150 --> 21:38.670
Really?

21:38.670 --> 21:41.840
Even if you go to a normal 
school and not music school?

21:42.540 --> 21:43.720
Why?

21:46.500 --> 21:48.780
I mean, don't you think 
we'll stop seeing each other

21:48.780 --> 21:52.010
if we go to different colleges 
unless we have a reason not to?

21:53.230 --> 21:56.460
Is that why you've been telling 
me to go to music school?

21:57.040 --> 21:58.250
Jeez, no.

22:01.140 --> 22:02.550
Why are you laughing?

22:02.550 --> 22:04.750
No, you're just so cute.

22:04.750 --> 22:06.150
You're making fun of me!

22:06.150 --> 22:07.460
I'm not! I'm not!

22:07.460 --> 22:08.440
I mean that as a compliment.

22:08.760 --> 22:10.320
It's true, though.

22:10.320 --> 22:14.900
Even if I ever want to meet up, 
you might not want to anymore.

22:15.380 --> 22:18.140
Especially if we go to different schools.

22:20.840 --> 22:22.470
You might be right.

22:23.130 --> 22:25.920
But I tend to think we'll be all right.

22:26.640 --> 22:27.910
How come?

22:29.070 --> 22:33.000
Do you think what we have 
together is special?

22:33.550 --> 22:35.690
Of course it is.

22:35.690 --> 22:37.790
That's why we're both here right now.

22:38.220 --> 22:39.160
Yeah.

22:39.160 --> 22:40.310
That's why.

22:45.680 --> 22:47.630
Actually, I wanna hit up the food stalls.

22:48.590 --> 22:49.780
Nice.

22:56.350 --> 22:57.570
Goldfish?

22:57.570 --> 22:58.360
Yeah.

22:58.860 --> 23:00.730
I caught them at the Agata Festival.

23:00.730 --> 23:02.030
Wow.

23:02.030 --> 23:04.690
That's out of character.

23:05.320 --> 23:06.750
I guess it's a keepsake.

23:07.190 --> 23:09.620
For the last Agata Festival 
of my high school life.

23:19.370 --> 23:24.960
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:21.960 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
